---
// Start a business outside Morgantown: Star City, Granville, Westover and
// places outside any town (#640, part of #277). Which town you are in decides
// the local license and B&O form. Each town's part comes from its own site.
// Westover is page text, not a record, until the city-of-westover org lands
// (PR #675). Fees, rates and due dates are left off: no town page states them.
// Waits for David (tax).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import SourceLine from '../components/SourceLine.astro';
import { resource, telHref } from '../lib/content.mjs';
export const page = { door: "family", topic: "work", label: "Start a business in Star City, Granville or Westover", summary: "Which town you are in decides the local business license and B&O tax form" };
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const westover = [{ url: 'https://www.westoverwv.org/new-businesses', checked: '2026-10-30' }];
---
<Base title="Start a business in Star City, Granville or Westover, Mon County, WV" description="Which town your business is in decides the local business license and B&O tax form. The Star City, Granville and Westover forms and offices, and who to ask outside any town in Monongalia County.">
  <h1>Start a business in Star City, Granville or Westover</h1>
  <p class="lede">Businesses in West Virginia register with the state first. After that, the town your business is in decides which local license and B&O (business and occupation) tax form you need. Check which town your business is in. Each part below comes from that town's own website.</p>
  <p>State registration and free help: see <a href={`${base}/business/`}>Start or grow a business</a>. Inside Morgantown city limits: see the city's <a href="https://www.morgantownwv.gov/247/Steps-to-Starting-Your-Business">Steps to Starting Your Business</a>.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={[{ url: 'https://www.morgantownwv.gov/247/Steps-to-Starting-Your-Business', checked: '2026-10-30' }]} about="Morgantown steps to starting a business" />

  <h2>Star City</h2>
  {resource('star-city-business-registration') && <ResourceCard r={resource('star-city-business-registration')} />}

  <h2>Granville</h2>
  {resource('granville-business-license') && <ResourceCard r={resource('granville-business-license')} />}

  <h2>Westover</h2>
  <article class="card resource" id="westover-new-businesses">
    <h3>Westover business forms</h3>
    <p>The City of Westover asks new businesses to call <a href={telHref('304-296-6860')}>(304) 296-6860</a> to get started. It also asks you to read its New Business Packet. Its New Businesses page lists these forms:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Business Registration Form</li>
      <li>Business License Application</li>
      <li>Business and Occupation (Gross Sales) Tax</li>
      <li>Homeland Security and MECCA 9-1-1 Registration</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Contractor, building permit and Certificate of Occupancy forms are on the same page. The page does not list fees or rates. City office: 500 Dupont Road, Westover. Paperwork questions: cityofwestover@westoverwv.gov.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="https://www.westoverwv.org/new-businesses"><span>Westover business forms</span></a></p>
    <SourceLine sources={westover} about="Westover business forms" />
  </article>

  <h2>Outside any town</h2>
  {resource('mon-county-planning-permits') && <ResourceCard r={resource('mon-county-planning-permits')} />}

  <p class="meta">Sources checked October 30, 2026. None of these town pages list license fees, B&O rates or due dates, so call the town office before you pay or file. We describe the steps; we do not decide what applies to your business. Something out of date? <a href="https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml">Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
